MV_WAIT_VB      equ 150              ; VBLANKs of dwell before it rises (PLATWAIT)
; The floor engine is MV_NMAX slots wide, laid out like the doors: parallel
; byte arrays indexed by the slot, not one set of scalars. It used to be a
; SINGLE mover, and E1M4 is what that costs -- 3 WR lifts, 3 switch lifts and 4
; lowering floors, of which only one could ever be in motion; every other lift
; and switch in the level was dead for the ~7 s a ride takes.
MV_NMAX     equ 20                   ; concurrent movers. Was 4 while a RAISE
                                     ;   finished on its first step; now that
                                     ;   stairs creep up (state 4, mv_raise) every
                                     ;   step holds a slot for its whole climb,
                                     ;   and EV_BuildStairs arms the WHOLE flight
                                     ;   in one press: E1M8's is 14 steps, E1M3's
                                     ;   10. 20 leaves room for a lift or a door
                                     ;   floor running alongside them.
