; mv_sector's DEPTH GUARD (movers.asm). Its BSP descent had no bound at all: it
; followed child indices until one had bit15 set, and when the node data forms a
; cycle it never does. That is not hypothetical -- an Altirra trace of a frozen
; LOAD (2026-08-26) shows $A114..$A131 repeating with identical registers, i.e.
; a node whose child is itself, and the machine is gone. DOOM can walk unbounded
; because it trusts its own tree; this port cannot. 40 levels is far past any
; real depth for these maps, so a bail-out only ever happens on bad data, and it
; bails to ?leaf -- the walk returns A sector instead of hanging the frame.
; Both call sites are three bytes for three: mv_sector's `lda MAP_HROOT` becomes
; `jsr mv_start` (which ends in that same lda) and its `jmp ?w` becomes
; `jmp mv_guard`, so its block does not grow by a byte.
