;==============================================================
; WEAPONS (weapon.asm, tools/pack_weap.py) -- the player's psprites
;--------------------------------------------------------------
;   DOOM keeps the gun in the player's hands OUT of the world: two "player
;   sprites" (ps_weapon + ps_flash) driven by their own state machine in
;   p_pspr.c, drawn by R_DrawPSprite at a fixed screen position. The port keeps
;   all of that 1:1 -- the same states, the same tic durations, the same
;   raise/lower/bob arithmetic (WEAPONTOP/BOTTOM, LOWERSPEED, MAXBOB) -- and only
;   changes where the numbers come from:
;     * the projection is PRECOMPUTED (pack_weap.py): every frame's record
;       carries its screen byte-column and row, so drawing is ONE BLT_BSTENCIL
;       rectangle through hud_blit's BCB. No per-column work at all.
;     * the state machine is ticked at DOOM's 35 Hz, not once per frame: wp_think
;       converts the frame's VBLANKs (dt_vbl) into tics (TIC_Q8) and runs that many
;       iterations, so the animation, the raise/lower slide and the bob keep
;       DOOM's timing at any frame rate -- the same reason the doors and lifts
;       count VBLANKs instead of frames.
;   NOT ported (there is nothing to shoot yet -- no monsters, no P_LineAttack):
;   the hitscan itself. Firing spends ammo, animates, flashes and sounds; it
;   leaves no puff and does no damage. That lands with the monsters.
;==============================================================
WEAPON_BASE     equ $F280            ; wp_think + the state tables + WEAP_TAB:
WEAPON_END      equ $F6E5            ;   under-ROM (cold: ~20 table steps a frame),
                                     ; 2026-08-28: was $F71B, which is a LIE for
                                     ; the SECOND time -- use_locate is parked at
                                     ; USELOC_BASE $F6E6-$F71B, inside the range
                                     ; this equ claimed, so WEAP_TAB grew 14 B
                                     ; into it and the `ert` said nothing. What
                                     ; caught it was check_xex.py's segment
                                     ; overlap test, which is the guard that
                                     ; actually knows where things landed. The
                                     ; lesson is the one written below in 2026-07
                                     ; and not learnt: THE REAL CEILING IS THE
                                     ; NEXT ORG, and there are two of them here
                                     ; (use_locate at $F6E6, update_flash at
                                     ; $F71C), not one.
                                     ; 2026-07-30: was $F7FF, which is a LIE --
                                     ; update_flash orgs at FLASH_BASE $F71C and
                                     ; en_bthings at $F78A, both INSIDE that range,
                                     ; so the ert guard let the state table grow
                                     ; 13 B into fl_tic with no error at all (MADS
                                     ; does not check segment overlap, and neither
                                     ; does check_xex.py -- it only knows RESERVED).
                                     ; The real ceiling is the next org, so that is
                                     ; what it says now.
                                     ;   in the big free block above read_keys and
                                     ;   below doors.asm ($F800)
