;   Each distinct column of a texture is stored in VRAM once and every column of
;   the texture carries a byte saying which stored one it is. 14-34 % of the
;   pixels per level, 23 % over episode 1 (tools/_tex_dedup.py) -- E1M3, the
;   level that sizes the 212 KB slot, goes 214,784 -> 175,312 B.
;   The index has to be read by the 6502 once per drawn column, so it lives in
;   ordinary RAM. It gets there WITHOUT a new ATR region: it rides at the front
;   of the .tex blob (which already streams per level) and diskio.asm's
;   tex_getix copies it back out of the MEMAC window right after the load. The
;   texture pixels therefore start at $018000 + TEXIX_MAX, not at $018000.
